usage: windows-tls-business-probe.py [-h] [--ssh-target SSH_TARGET]
                                     [--identity IDENTITY] [--exe EXE]
                                     [--report REPORT]
                                     [--web-bundle WEB_BUNDLE] [--browser]
                                     [--browser-content {HOMEWORK,REMINDER}]
                                     [--continuous-accept]
                                     [--visual-fixture {FILLED_DEFAULT,FILLED_ZERO,OUTLINED}]
                                     [--voice-capabilities] [--visual-only]
                                     [--header-deadline-only] [--self-test]

Run the explicit finite TLS/shared-worker synthetic business diagnostic. The
default is a raw API client through an owned SSH forward. Optional --header-
deadline-only samples actual TLS/raw incomplete-header closure within an
unrounded conservative pre-connect5s bound; it does not replace the original
strict-P0 decision or establish kernel timestamps. Optional --browser also
observes actual isolated Windows Edge UI against the same native service. This
is not general browser acceptance, production-listener enablement, native
strict-5s evidence, audio playback, or Windows 7/10 compatibility evidence.
Project code runs only from the supplied diagnostic EXE; --browser uses the
separately owned installed Edge process. The disposable public certificate is
trusted in this Python context only; its private key never leaves Windows and
no system trust/network setting is changed.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --ssh-target SSH_TARGET
  --identity IDENTITY
  --exe EXE
  --report REPORT
  --web-bundle WEB_BUNDLE
                        Existing development ZIP; only verified web manifest
                        payloads are uploaded
  --browser             Also verify isolated Windows Edge UI against this same
                        finite native service
  --browser-content {HOMEWORK,REMINDER}
                        Explicit isolated browser journey; REMINDER uses the
                        real bottom shortcut and no subject-visual requests
  --continuous-accept   Also verify real idle AcceptEx repost and four
                        admitted JSON bodies within the original client/native
                        deadlines; not strict TCP5s evidence
  --visual-fixture {FILLED_DEFAULT,FILLED_ZERO,OUTLINED}
                        Exact finite isolated synthetic display fixture; no
                        production settings
  --voice-capabilities  Also observe three real capability GETs after pairing;
                        no new audio operation or native-query/cache-count
                        inference
  --visual-only         Target only visual/scope/read-only contract within the
                        original client/native budgets
  --header-deadline-only
                        Explicit finite four incomplete TLS heads then one raw
                        TCP deadline sample; original5e9ns conservative pre-
                        connect bound, not production/ESTABLISHED
                        certification
  --self-test
